######################################################################
# Database to simulate 
#
# MF6PQC adaptation:
# PHT3D stores NAPL and SRB as immobile kinetic components outside
# PHREEQC. Here they are native PHREEQC KINETICS reactants. NAPL rates
# therefore use M, and the Sulfred rate combines growth saved by the eight
# hydrocarbon rates with first-order decay. This preserves immobility while
# the 29 aqueous components are transported by MODFLOW 6.
#
# LNAPL (BTEX + selected PAHs) dissolution, 
# microbially mediate degradation under sulphate reducing
# conditions and the corresponding geochemical changes (minerals).
# carbon isotope fractionation for BTEX/PAH
# sulfate isotope fractionation
# - Lowsolubnapl represents less/nonsoluble compounds in the NAPL mix 
# - dissolution for BTEX/PAH compounds is a fraction of the single-species 
#   solubility - determined by parm(1)  
# - dissolution of Lowsolubnapl is neglected
# - redox state of nitrogen is fixed
#
# Details for modelling of microbially mediated BTEX degradation under 
# sulfate-reducing conditions are given in
# Prommer, H., Barry, D.A., and Davis, G. B. (2002). 
# Modelling of physical and reactive processes 
# during biodegradation of a hydrocarbon plume under transient 
# groundwater flow conditions. 
# J. Cont. Hydrol. 59, 113-131.
######################################################################

